sort - sort lines of text

SYNOPSIS
    sort [-r] [file]

DESCRIPTION
    Read lines from file or standard input and write them in ascending byte
    order. Use -r for descending order. The input is held in memory. Each
    line can contain up to 4095 bytes before its newline.

EXAMPLES
    sort names | uniq

SEE ALSO
    cut(1), uniq(1)
